      "writtenOn": "2015-09-01T10:09:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I see what you are doing - so you want to authenticate and authorize user at this early stage because the whole call (I deducted this from the curl -X GET keystone/v3/auth/tokens example in the doc) is a token validation, so you must provide a token to validate.\n\nWhat is we used cul -X POST /auth/tokens with the certificate, and in the AuthContextMiddleware simply build a json object so it looks like it was a federation request - something like this: https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/contrib/federation/controllers.py#L280\n\nPlease, explain if I am missing something :-)\nP.S. Looking at the class name (AuthCoontextMiddleware) and the place where it is called in the pipe, it\u0027s purpose seems to  build auth context, not authenticate the user.",
      "revId": "3c01f8762855e47f34823b76f5fd4a8780704718",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da20952f_7fe48cab",
        "filename": "keystone/middleware/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 58
      },
      "lineNbr": 251,
      "author": {
        "id": 1916
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-09-01T23:56:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are not authenticating the user. Like federation, user is authenticated if 2-Way SSL session is successfully establish. We are simple using the mapping to determine the certificate\u0027s authorization attributes.\n\nIf someone is calling \u0027curl -X POST /auth/tokens\u0027, they meant to get a token. In this case, if the accidentally use the cert in which we allow for tokenless authz, the auth context will still get built. But needless to say, it is redundent.\n\nTokenless authz is not meant for token request. It is intended to replaced the need for token request in order to perform the privilege operations.",
      "parentUuid": "da20952f_848cdeda",
      "revId": "3c01f8762855e47f34823b76f5fd4a8780704718",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
